Compact release analysis JSON follows:
{{ analysis_json }}

The harness recreated `{{ release_branch }}` on fresh `{{ base_branch }}` and
kept every prior immutable release ref unchanged.
{{ if candidate_tree_notes -}}
It folded the fresh candidate tree's complete `## Unreleased` and
`changelog.d` content into `## v{{ target_version }}`.
{{ else -}}
It restored the frozen release body for `## v{{ target_version }}` and retained
later base-branch notes in `## Unreleased` for the next release.
{{ end -}}

Perform one bounded evidence pass:

- `release_read CHANGELOG.md` to inspect the prepared release section and note
  state.
- `release_run` with
  `git log --oneline {{ recovery_oid }}..origin/{{ base_branch }}` to classify
  changes that landed after the recovery commit.
- `release_search` for one representative release-note entry and inspect the
  corresponding source or diff.

Return one short `Audit:` block. Do not produce a draft changelog.
